<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Robots on Earth and in Space – Lesson # 4</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Robots on Earth and in Space</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How Robots Are Used in Panama</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop short reports on general interest subjects. Interactive: Provide feedback on narrative writing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can develop a report on robotics used in Panama and speculate on future applications (e.g., "I researched how robots are used in Panama's agriculture to automate harvesting. In the future, robots could also assist with planting and monitoring crops in remote areas.")
Can edit narratives on futuristic space exploration topics, focusing on detail and coherence (e.g., "I think you could make the story more interesting by adding details about the sounds and sights astronauts experience on a space mission.")
Can provide written feedback on reports, assessing clarity and detail (e.g., "Your report is clear, but I think you should add more specific examples, like how robots are currently used in Panama's healthcare system to assist with surgery.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of various robots used in different Panamanian industries (e.g., agriculture, medicine, logistics). Students are asked to quickly jot down 2-3 sentences describing one of the images, focusing on what the robot does or could do. This activates prior knowledge and sets a writing context. Students are encouraged to use vocabulary related to <i>robot, technology, agriculture, medicine, industry</i>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to write a descriptive sentence using a visual prompt. For example, pointing to an image of an agricultural robot, the teacher says: "This <b>robot</b> is used in <b>agriculture</b> to automate harvesting. It collects data efficiently." The teacher explicitly models the pronunciation of /r/ in "robot" and "research", and /s/ in "sensors" and "space", reinforcing these sounds. The teacher also demonstrates how to form a sentence in the passive voice related to scientific reporting: "Data <i>is collected by</i> robots for analysis."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main purpose of our writing activity today?" (Expected answer: "To describe how robots are used in Panama.")</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When we talk about 'automation,' what does that mean a robot helps do?" (Expected answer: "It means the robot performs tasks without human intervention, making things more efficient.")</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Robots on Earth and in Space")</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informational article excerpt (approx. 150 words) from a scientific journal or news report, titled "Robotics in Panama: A Glimpse into the Future". The article describes current uses of robots in Panamanian sectors like <i>agriculture, medicine</i>, and <i>logistics</i>, and briefly touches upon future potential, linking to <i>space exploration</i> technologies. It includes examples of data being <i>collected</i>, machines being <i>operated</i>, and benefits like increased <i>efficiency</i> and <i>safety</i>. It incorporates passive voice and future perfect examples.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Identifies key information and arguments in short descriptive reports and articles about technological advancements.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the article individually. Then, they complete the following in writing:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> What is the main idea of this article about robots in Panama? (Students write a one-sentence answer.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Read the following statements and write "True" or "False" based on the article.
                    <ol>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Robots are currently only used in Panama's factories.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">By 2030, robots will have transformed the medical industry in Panama.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Data for environmental research is collected by drones.</li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using the Future perfect for discussing technology impacts, Passive voice for scientific reporting, and Zero conditional for cause-effect scenarios. Target vocabulary includes: <i>robot, technology, automation, industry, agriculture, medicine, factory, machine, program, control, sensor, repair, safety, space, astronaut, satellite, rocket, launch, operate, explore, collect, efficient, automated</i>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides sentence starters or gaps, and students complete them using the target grammar and vocabulary.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"By 2035, robots _______ (transform) how <b>agriculture</b> is managed in Panama." (Students write: "will have transformed")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Important <b>data</b> _______ (collect) by the <b>sensors</b> on the exploration <b>robot</b>." (Students write: "is collected")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a <b>machine</b> _______ (program) correctly, it _______ (perform) with high <b>precision</b>." (Students write: "is programmed, it performs")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The <b>rocket</b> _______ (launch) next year to orbit the new <b>satellite</b>." (Students write: "will be launched") - *Practice pronunciation of -ed endings for past participles: "programmed" (/d/), "launched" (/t/).*</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation):</b> In pairs, students receive a set of active voice sentences or simple present tense sentences about robots. They rewrite them using passive voice or future perfect.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1 (Passive): "Engineers often <b>repair</b> the industrial <b>robots</b>." (Students rewrite: "The industrial <b>robots</b> are often <b>repaired</b> by engineers.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2 (Future Perfect): "The company introduces new <b>automation technology</b> next year." (Students rewrite: "By next year, the company <b>will have introduced</b> new <b>automation technology</b>.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3 (Zero Conditional): "If astronauts <b>explore</b> an unexplored <b>planet</b>, they <b>discover</b> new forms of life." (Students rewrite: "If <b>astronauts</b> explore an <b>unexplored planet</b>, they often <b>discover</b> new forms of life.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Paragraph Writing:</b> Still in pairs, students write a short paragraph (3-4 sentences) describing a potential future application of robots in a specific sector in Panama (e.g., healthcare, infrastructure, space research collaboration). They must use at least one instance of the future perfect, one passive voice construction, and one zero conditional. They are encouraged to offer solutions in their discussions and consider different viewpoints.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Report Writing and Peer Editing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in groups of three. Each group will divide into two sub-tasks:</p>
            <ol>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 1: Report on Robotics in Panama (Writing – Productive):</b> Two students from each group will collaboratively write a short report (approx. 100-120 words) detailing how robots are currently used in *one specific sector* in Panama (e.g., *agriculture, medicine, industry*) and speculate on *future applications*. They must integrate at least two instances of the passive voice for scientific reporting and two instances of the future perfect to discuss future impacts. They should also include relevant vocabulary like *automation, efficiency, sensor, control, program*. They need to ensure their report is clear and includes specific examples. The teacher emphasizes encouraging respectful dialogue on diverse perspectives regarding the impacts of robotics as they write.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 2: Narrative Peer Editing (Writing – Interactive):</b> The third student in the group will receive a short, pre-written (by the teacher) futuristic narrative excerpt (approx. 80-100 words) about space exploration (e.g., an <b>astronaut's mission</b> to an <b>unexplored planet</b>, using a <b>rocket</b> or <b>satellite</b> for <b>research</b>). This student's task is to provide written feedback on the narrative, focusing on detail, coherence, and suggesting ways to make the story more interesting. They should use phrases like, "I think you could add more details about..." or "Perhaps you could make this part clearer by...". After 10 minutes, the roles within the group rotate so everyone gets a chance to participate in both writing and editing.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The goal is to produce a coherent report and provide constructive feedback on a narrative, demonstrating the learning outcomes for productive and interactive writing.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer Assessment with a Checklist and Teacher Observation.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will submit their group's final report on robotics in Panama and the peer feedback on the futuristic narrative. Each group will use a simple checklist to evaluate another group's report, providing constructive written comments.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (for the report):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the report (well-organized ideas).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of at least two passive voice constructions.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of at least two future perfect constructions.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>robot, technology, agriculture, medicine, automation, efficient</i>).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of specific examples or speculation for future applications.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">For peer feedback: Constructive, detailed, and polite suggestions.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short reflection on a sticky note:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new thing I learned about writing reports on robotics today is..."</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I still need practice with..." (e.g., passive voice, future perfect, specific vocabulary).</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Student and Teacher Reflection)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did giving and receiving feedback on narratives help you understand what makes good written work?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What challenges did your group face while writing the report about robots in Panama, and how did you overcome them?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., collaborative report writing, peer editing structure, integration of specific grammar).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled with the grammar points or report structure in the next writing task? (e.g., providing more sentence frames, mini-grammar review, clearer examples of strong reports).</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use the reports and narrative ideas developed in this lesson to create a multimedia presentation or a summary for a wider audience, demonstrating their 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
    </tr>
</table>